# Where the workflows find MIRAL Soft's own downloads, and which CatalogTool they use. One place
# for both (C-09); changing either is an ordinary pull request.
#
# DEPLOY_BASE   the address of the download host, ending in "/". It moves when the hosting
#               does; the catalog's own mirror address is mirrorBase in settings.json.
# CATALOGTOOL_DIR
#               the folder below <DEPLOY_BASE>catalogtool/: "test/<commit>" for a test build
#               made from a commit of MIRAL-Deploy, "<version>" for a release. A test build never
#               lies in a version folder, so it cannot be mistaken for a release.
# CATALOGTOOL_VERSION
#               the version the tool must name when it starts.
# CATALOGTOOL_*_SHA256
#               the SHA-256 of the two files; the trust comes from these, not from the host.
DEPLOY_BASE=https://deploy.miralsoft.com/
CATALOGTOOL_DIR=test/e80fe75
CATALOGTOOL_VERSION=0.1.0
CATALOGTOOL_LINUX_SHA256=9e1ec655867331dfd2dd5f3813aa263b063cd04f762eecb162b986815cac847b
CATALOGTOOL_WINDOWS_SHA256=0b852730df827fe003975354c6ab8c1f5aeac5bca9daa6f078dff3473a01aee8
